<article class="env-lemma" id="09VR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09VR">Lemma <span data-tag="09VR">7.22.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{D}$ be sites and let $v : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}$ be a continuous functor. Assume $v$ has a left adjoint $u : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$u$ is cocontinuous, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the results of Lemmas <a href="/tag/00XX" data-tag="00XX">7.22.1</a> and <a href="/tag/00XY" data-tag="00XY">7.22.2</a> hold. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In particular, $v$ defines a morphism of sites $f : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}$ and let $\{ V_ j \to u(U)\} _{j \in J}$ be a covering in $\mathcal{D}$. Then $\{ v(V_ j) \to v(u(U))\} _{i \in I}$ is a covering in $\mathcal{C}$. Via the adjunction map $U \to v(u(U))$ we can base change this to a covering $\{ W_ j \to U\} _{j \in J}$ with $W_ j = v(V_ j) \times _{v(u(U))} U$. Denoting $p_ j : W_ j \to v(V_ j)$ the first projection, we obtain maps 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  u(W_ j) \xrightarrow {u(p_ j)} u(v(V_ j)) \longrightarrow V_ j  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the second arrow is the adjunction map. This determines a morphism $\{ u(W_ j) \to u(U)\}  \to \{ V_ j \to u(U)\} $ of families of maps with fixed target, showing that $u$ is indeed cocontinuous. The other statements are immediate from Lemmas <a href="/tag/00XX" data-tag="00XX">7.22.1</a> and <a href="/tag/00XY" data-tag="00XY">7.22.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>